  "notes": "The research defines this entry entirely by contrast — \"harder-drum counterpart to 9th Wonder's soul school\", \"harder and drier than his Jamla peers\", \"drums clearly above the loop\" — so the parameters that matter are the ones that read against 9th Wonder. `velocityTiers` is raised where 9th Wonder's is lowered, the snare keeps its rimshot layer and a 0.28 ghost probability where 9th Wonder's is 0.15, the kick runs 3–4 hits a bar rather than 2–4, and `hihat.fillDensity` is 0.48 against his 0.35. The chops \"retain the source's instrumental colour rather than vocals\", which is why the melody is a horn/Rhodes line at ordinary density rather than a re-sequenced vocal slice pile. ⚠ `session.swing` is deliberately inherited rather than authored: the research says \"8th hats with swing\" and nothing more, and the genre's 0.58 already is that. Inventing a number would have been an invention. ⚠ `medium` and the research says medium too — it is explicit that \"technical detail [is] thinner than his peers'\". The specific inferred parameter is `drums.velocityTiers`, which is this author's translation of \"drums clearly above the loop\" into the only lever a MIDI style model has. ⚠ The i–VII–VI family is INFERRED; the research names i–iv and ii–V–i. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 46 to 45 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 46 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 1.",
